{
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom:8.0pt;line-height:115%&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Aptos&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-hansi-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\nmso-font-kerning:1.0pt;mso-ligatures:standardcontextual;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US&quot;&gt;The proposed first floor rear extension in conjunction with the existing\r\nroof extensions on the host property,&amp;nbsp;by reason of its prominent siting, and\r\npoor and awkward design, would result in an inappropriate, obtrusive and\r\nincongruous roof form which would fail to respect the character and appearance\r\nof the dwellinghouse and the prevailing pattern of development in the area, to\r\nthe detriment of the character and appearance of the subject dwellinghouse and\r\nthe streetscene,. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the high quality\r\ndesign aspiration of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies\r\nD1, D3.D(1) and D3.D(11) of The London Plan (2021), core policy CS1.B of the\r\nHarrow Core Strategy (2021), Policy DM1 of the Development Management Policies\r\nLocal Plan document (2013) and the adopted Harrow Supplementary Planning\r\nDocument Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
